s=3D"note-content-field disable-tex-rendering">Comment:</strong> <div class=
=3D"note-content-value markdown-rendered"><p>Thank you for the clarificatio=
n. We state the motivation more directly.</p>
<p>Sharpness is closely connected to generalization and forgetting, which m=
akes its role in PECL an important open question rather than a minor implem=
entation issue. In frozen-backbone PECL, future adaptation is confined to a=
 low-rank admissible update subspace, so the flatness notion inherited from=
 full-parameter training is no longer automatically the right one. Until th=
is is clarified, flatness-based PECL remains partly heuristic: it is unclea=
r what should be perturbed, what curvature should be measured, and which ge=
ometry is actually relevant under subspace-constrained updates.</p>
<p>This is the gap our paper addresses. Our contribution is not to recommen=
d a more common SAM implementation, but to identify the sharpness object th=
at is theoretically relevant in frozen-backbone PECL. Concretely, our analy=
sis shows that the bound-relevant sharpness term and the KL complexity are =
supported on the admissible update space <mjx-container class=3D"MathJax Ct=
xtMenu_Attached_0" jax=3D"CHTML" tabindex=3D"0" ctxtmenu_counter=3D"5" styl=
e=3D"font-size: 121.3%; position: relative;"><mjx-math class=3D"MJX-TEX" ar=
ia-hidden=3D"true"><mjx-msub><mjx-mi class=3D"mjx-i"><mjx-c class=3D"mjx-c1=
