<blockquote>
<p>Limited scalability: Does this analysis hold regardless of model complex=
ity or model size?
Could the authors provide additional empirical data covering various model =
architectures and scales?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>To test whether the effect persists across architecture family and model=
 scale, we additionally evaluate T5-small and T5-large on a standard NLP co=
ntinual-learning benchmark (AG News, Amazon Reviews, DBpedia, Yahoo Answers=
) under three task orders [1]. We use Adam as the common base optimizer for=
 both the baseline and AS(0), since Adam-style optimization is standard for=
 T5-based PEFT. Here AS(0)denotes adapter-scoped SAM with Adam as the base =
optimizer, thus the comparison isolates the effect of the perturabtion. We =
use this as a targeted cross-architecture/scale check, not as a second full=
 scope/type ablation.</p>
<p>The same qualitative trend remains: AS(0) improves over Adam on both mod=
el scales, especially on T5-large. This provides additional evidence that t=
he benefit of adapter-scoped sharpness is not limited to the original ViT-B=
