ote-content-container "><div class=3D"note-content"><div><strong class=3D"n=
ote-content-field disable-tex-rendering">Summary:</strong> <div class=3D"no=
te-content-value markdown-rendered"><p>This paper explores the interaction =
between sharpness-aware optimization and low-rank subspace constraints (e.g=
., LoRA) in Parameter Efficient Continuous Learning (PECL). The authors not=
e that traditional sharpness-aware methods perturb the entire parameter spa=
ce, creating a disconnect with PECL's dynamics, which updates only within t=
ask-specific subspaces. To address this, the paper introduces the concept o=
f =E2=80=9CSubspace Sharpness=E2=80=9D and derives a novel sequential hiera=
rchical PAC-Bayesian generalization bound. Theoretical analysis demonstrate=
s that controlling sharpness within the subspace suffices to provide genera=
lization guarantees when the backbone network is frozen. Experiments valida=
te that applying first-order sharpness minimization (AS-1) within task-perm=
issible subspaces significantly enhances continuous learning accuracy and m=
itigates forgetting across multiple LoRA variants (SeqLoRA, IncLoRA, OLORA)=
.</p>
</div></div><div><strong class=3D"note-content-field disable-tex-rendering"=
>Strengths And Weaknesses:</strong> <div class=3D"note-content-value markdo=
wn-rendered"><p>Strengths:</p>
<ol>
<li>The paper proposes a sequential hierarchical PAC-Bayesian analysis fram=
ework that provides theoretical guarantees.</li>
<li>Extensive experiments across multiple benchmarks are conducted to demon=
strate the effectiveness of the proposed method.</li>
</ol>
<p>Weaknesses:</p>
<ol>
<li>The motivation of the paper is not entirely convincing. Applying AS(1) =
perturbation only to the LoRA adapter appears to be the standard way of usi=
ng SAM, and this practice does not seem to introduce the claimed perturbati=
on misalignment issue. Moreover, the empirical results presented in the pap=
er suggest that this default strategy is already the most effective.</li>
<li>The paper should discuss prior work that applies PAC-Bayesian analysis =
to continual learning, such as [1] and [2].</li>
<li>Additional PEFT approaches should be included to better validate the ef=
fectiveness of the proposed subspace-restricted updates.</li>
<li>Some notations are used before being defined. For example, <mjx-contain=
er class=3D"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0" jax=3D"CHTML" tabindex=3D"0" ctxtm=
enu_counter=3D"41" style=3D"font-size: 121.3%; position: relative;"><mjx-ma=
th class=3D"MJX-TEX" aria-hidden=3D"true"><mjx-texatom texclass=3D"ORD"><mj=
