div class=3D"note-content"><div><strong class=3D"note-content-field disable=
-tex-rendering">Rebuttal:</strong> <div class=3D"note-content-value markdow=
n-rendered"><blockquote>
<p>The motivation of the paper is not entirely convincing. Applying AS(1) p=
erturbation only to the LoRA adapter appears to be the standard way of usin=
g SAM, and this practice does not seem to introduce the claimed perturbatio=
n misalignment issue. </p>
</blockquote>
<p>The misalignment we refer to is not within adapter-only AS(1), but betwe=
en full-scope sharpness and the admissible LoRA update space in frozen-back=
bone PECL. Adapter-scoped AS(1) is the strongest strategy in our experiment=
s, but prior work does not establish a PECL-specific criterion explaining w=
hy this is the correct sharpness notion.</p>
<p>The motivation comes from a genuine tension between settings. Flat-LoRA =
[1], developed in the standard fine-tuning setting, argues that LoRA can st=
ill induce sharpness in the full parameter space. Accordingly, it enforces =
flatness through perturbations of the merged weights in the full parameter =
space. In PECL, however, updates are structurally confined to the admissibl=
e LoRA subspace across tasks, so the relevant sharpness object is no longer=
 obvious. Adapter-only perturbation may seem intuitively plausible, but thi=
s does not by itself explain why the PECL-relevant sharpness should be the =
subspace-restricted one rather than the full-model one.</p>
<p>Theorem 4.4 provides that criterion. Once the PAC-Bayesian bound is spec=
ialized to frozen-backbone PECL, both the KL-complexity term and the sharpn=
ess-dependent empirical loss reduce to perturbations supported on <mjx-cont=
ainer class=3D"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0" jax=3D"CHTML" tabindex=3D"0" ct=
xtmenu_counter=3D"42" style=3D"font-size: 121.3%; position: relative;"><mjx=
-math class=3D"MJX-TEX" aria-hidden=3D"true"><mjx-msub><mjx-mi class=3D"mjx=
-i"><mjx-c class=3D"mjx-c1D44A TEX-I"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=3D=
"vertical-align: -0.153em; margin-left: -0.104em;"><mjx-texatom size=3D"s" =
texclass=3D"ORD"><mjx-mi class=3D"mjx-n"><mjx-c class=3D"mjx-c394"></mjx-c>=
</mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=3D"mjx-n"><mjx-c class=3D"mjx-c2C"></mjx-c></mjx-mo>=
<mjx-mi class=3D"mjx-i"><mjx-c class=3D"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I"></mjx-c></mjx-mi>=
</mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msub></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselec=
