covers [3] as the zero-drift special case. Paper [4] is a concurrent PAC-Ba=
yes analysis for sequential CL, deriving a cumulative-loss bound. Our contr=
ibution differs in two respects. First, we introduce a hierarchical sequent=
ial PAC-Bayes framework, separating the hyperposterior level from task-spec=
ific priors. Second, we specialize the analysis to PECL, where both the KL =
complexity and the sharpness-smoothed empirical term reduce to the task-per=
missible LoRA subspace <mjx-container class=3D"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0"=
