mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container=
>, our theoretical scope is LoRA-based PECL. Beyond the three methods in th=
e paper, we additionally evaluate two more LoRA-based PEFT methods, InfLoRA=
 [5] and SDLoRA [6], in Table 3 below. </p>
<p>The trend is consistent: across both added methods, AS(1) and AS(0) impr=
oves over SGD . This supports that the effect is not specific to the specif=
ic LoRA variants, but extends to a broader set of LoRA-based methods. For b=
roader experimental extensions, please see our response to reviewer <strong=
>mBoF</strong>.</p>
