<p>Our motivation is the same core issue clarified above: in frozen-backbon=
e PECL, future adaptation is restricted to a low-rank admissible update spa=
ce, so the flatness notion inherited from full-parameter training is no lon=
ger automatically appropriate. Without resolving this point, flatness-based=
 PECL remains partly heuristic, because it is unclear which perturbations, =
curvature, and geometry are actually relevant to generalization and forgett=
ing.</p>
<p>Our paper addresses this missing criterion. The goal is not to show that=
 adapter-only SAM can work, but to identify which sharpness notion is theor=
etically relevant under PECL constraints. Our analysis shows that, in froze=
n-backbone PECL, the bound-relevant sharpness term and KL complexity are su=
pported on the admissible update space <mjx-container class=3D"MathJax Ctxt=
Menu_Attached_0" jax=3D"CHTML" tabindex=3D"0" ctxtmenu_counter=3D"46" style=
=3D"font-size: 121.3%; position: relative;"><mjx-math class=3D"MJX-TEX" ari=
